    "release_notes": "FOODEX 1.0.109: Make FOODEX Assistant genuinely hybrid: the deterministic brain remains the always-available parser/fallback while the Agent Orchestrator exclusively owns external-AI planning and synthesis, avoiding duplicate provider routing calls in one turn. Answer safe general/non-live questions directly with the configured AI provider instead of forcing a Database fallback; live FOODEX business facts still require authorized server tools and cannot be invented by the model. Add bounded direct-AI repair when a general provider reply does not follow the planner schema, while preserving scope-denial fail-closed behavior and preventing AI from claiming database access or completed mutations. Generate 2-4 contextual follow-up prompts from AI for both direct replies and grounded FOODEX answers; suggestions are localized, deduplicated, length-bounded and rendered fresh per reply. Preserve AI vs Database provenance: tool/evidence-backed answers remain labeled Database, while tool-free successful model replies are labeled AI. Preserve RBAC, tenant/store/channel isolation, read-only enforcement, approval gates, provider budgets, Qwen3 low-reasoning mode, and the rule that chain-of-thought is never exposed or stored. Remove the hidden 6s/12s chat latency bottleneck that could make a CPU-hosted provider pass the Settings test but fall back during real conversations; allow the Agent turn to use up to 30 seconds while the provider request still respects the saved provider timeout and bounded Agent budget. Publish as Dashboard/backend-only 1.0.109 on top of 1.0.108; Customer, Driver and Van identities remain unchanged and are not rebuilt. Regenerate the canonical 1.0.109 Dashboard update bundle from the reconciled release head before final convergence to `main`, preserving exact-head release metadata and checksums."
